From: fpvOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] media: wave5: reset inherited AR9311 decoder state

AR9311 can enter through a stock-Linux RAM handoff with codec firmware
still running. Apply the existing encoder reset path to decoder probe too,
so no old firmware or DMA allocation is reused. Other platforms retain
their existing initialization behavior.

--- a/drivers/media/platform/chips-media/wave5/wave5-vpuapi.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/chips-media/wave5/wave5-vpuapi.c
@@ -25,7 +25,10 @@
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	if (wave5_vpu_is_init(vpu_dev) && !vpu_dev->artosyn_encoder) {
+	/* Stock Linux can leave firmware running across an AR9311 RAM handoff.
+	 * Reset it before assigning new code and DMA buffers, for either role.
+	 */
+	if (wave5_vpu_is_init(vpu_dev) && !vpu_dev->artosyn) {
 		wave5_vpu_re_init(dev, (void *)code, size);
 		ret = -EBUSY;
 		goto err_out;
